- **Why the kill bar triggers (known vs unseen machine topologies)**:
  - On the **48 items with known machine topologies** under held-out phrasing/templates/styles (`style|tape`, `style|num`, `tmpl|tape`, `tmpl|num`, `legacy|elevator`, `legacy|clock`), `r4` sampling lifts coverage from **$28/48$ ($58.3\%$) greedy to $39/48$ ($81.3\%$) at $T=0.7$ and $40/48$ ($83.3\%$) at $T=1.0$** ($41/48 = 85.4\%$ pooled; `legacy|clock` rises from $0/8 \to 8/8$).
  - On the **40 items with held-out machine topologies** (`kind|tape`, `kind|num`, `all3|tape`, `all3|num`, `legacy|pattern`), `r4` coverage is **$2/40$ ($5.0\%$) greedy and $4/40$ ($10.0\%$) at $T=0.7$ and $T=1.0$**. Temperature sampling cannot invent unseen state-transition structures when the policy places near-zero mass on them.
- **Disambiguation efficiency**: Whenever the intended transducer is in the sampled set, canonical minimisation ([`minimise_moore_reg`](file:///Users/neo/repos/polyformer-wt/askq/research/askq/askq_core.py#L169-L257), [`minimise_mealy_reg`](file:///Users/neo/repos/polyformer-wt/askq/research/askq/askq_core.py#L59-L133)) and generalised binary search ([`run_gbs`](file:///Users/neo/repos/polyformer-wt/askq/research/askq/askq_core.py#L415-L498)) isolate it in a median of **$0$–$1$ questions** (with $97.7\%$ of items at $T=0.7$ and $93.2\%$ at $T=1.0$ needing $\le 2$ questions, and $100\%$ of distinguishing words satisfying $|w| \le n_i + n_j - 1$).

#### 2. Per-Row Token Log-Probabilities of the Greedy Table (AUROC for Flagging Wrong Rows)

Computed via exact teacher-forced `torch.log_softmax` in [`compute_hf_call_logprobs`](file:///Users/neo/repos/polyformer-wt/askq/research/askq/askq_eval.py#L79-L110) and scored by [`summarize_row_auroc`](file:///Users/neo/repos/polyformer-wt/askq/research/askq/askq_core.py#L691-L719):
- **`r4` (`84` tables, `5,601` rows; `2,916` exact-wrong / `2,880` normalised-wrong)**:
  - **All rows**: `-mean_logprob` pooled AUROC $= \mathbf{0.5523}$ (exact) / $\mathbf{0.5475}$ (norm); within-table mean AUROC $= \mathbf{0.5427}$ / $\mathbf{0.5597}$ (`-rhs_logprob` within-table $= \mathbf{0.5546}$ / $\mathbf{0.5698}$).
  - **By arm**: On `tape` (Moore, $1,362$ rows), `-mean_logprob` has a real table-level signal (**pooled AUROC $= 0.7700$ / $0.7918$**, within-table `-rhs_logprob` AUROC $= 0.6104$ / $0.6318$); on 200-row `number` (Mealy, $4,239$ rows), the model emits wrong tables with $>99\%$ token confidence (**pooled AUROC $= 0.4952$**, **within-table AUROC $= 0.4807$**).
- **`reason-s1` (`78` tables, `6,599` rows; `4,391` exact-wrong / `4,359` normalised-wrong)**:
  - **All rows**: `-mean_logprob` pooled AUROC $= \mathbf{0.5565}$ (exact) / $\mathbf{0.5503}$ (norm); within-table mean AUROC $= \mathbf{0.5166}$ / $\mathbf{0.4909}$.
  - **By arm**: `tape` pooled AUROC $= \mathbf{0.7532}$ / $\mathbf{0.7424}$ (within-table $= 0.5904$ / $0.5264$); `number` pooled AUROC $= \mathbf{0.5882}$ (within-table $= 0.4492$).

